% NY N348144 (January 2026): a women's knit sweater from Cambodia.
scenario ny_n348144 is:
    style 239752 is an upper body garment, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 is classified under the US tariff, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    the fabric construction of style 239752 is knitted, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    the cut of style 239752 indicates women, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 contains 47.7 percent of cotton, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 contains 31.3 percent of polyester, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 contains 13.7 percent of nylon, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 contains 6.6 percent of elastane, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    style 239752 contains 0.7 percent of metalized yarn, as stated in ruling NY N348144.
    all the yarn of style 239752 is metalized yarn,
        according to the CBP laboratory, as stated in ruling NY N348144,
        because "the garment is knitted from a single eight-ply yarn with all plies, two of them metallic, twisted together".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style 239752 is 6110.90"].

