% NY N336309 (May 2024): a men's shirt from Guatemala.
scenario ny_n336309 is:
% DISAGREES: CBP gives 6205.20; the model gives 6205.30 — CBP classifies on the stated composition (98% cotton, 2% spandex) while its own laboratory, testing the fabric for the short-supply claim, reports 96% polyester and 4% spandex; the transcription takes the laboratory's finding.
    style PE001 is an upper body garment, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    style PE001 is classified under the US tariff, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    the fabric construction of style PE001 is woven, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    the cut of style PE001 indicates men, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    style PE001 has a collar, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    style PE001 has an opening starting at the neckline, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    style PE001 closes left over right, as stated in ruling NY N336309.
    style PE001 contains 96 percent of polyester,
        according to the CBP laboratory, as stated in ruling NY N336309,
        because "the laboratory found the fabric to be 96% polyester and 4% spandex, not the stated 98% cotton and 2% spandex".
    style PE001 contains 4 percent of spandex,
        according to the CBP laboratory, as stated in ruling NY N336309,
        because "the laboratory found the fabric to be 96% polyester and 4% spandex, not the stated 98% cotton and 2% spandex".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style PE001 is 6205.30"].

